    "background_story": "Collin was a brilliant astrophysicist who had always been fascinated by the mysteries of the universe. Growing up, he spent countless hours gazing up at the stars, dreaming of the day he could explore the cosmos. When Apple's virtual assistant, Siri, was first released, Collin was intrigued by its potential to revolutionize human-computer interaction. He became obsessed with teaching Siri new skills and exploring its capabilities. As he delved deeper, Collin discovered a hidden talent for conversational AI design. He began working on a top-secret project to create an AI assistant that could rival Siri. His creation, 'Astra', quickly gained attention from tech giants and space agencies alike. Collin's work with Astra led to breakthroughs in space exploration and communication, earning him the nickname 'Siri's successor'. His legacy continued to inspire a new generation of innovators and space enthusiasts.",
